# Final STRIDE rerun of the grammar-7 tree, Stellar testnet, 19 October 2026
#
# Tree: feat/grammar-v7 at 3624e930 (after #25, #27 and #26). Adapter v5 4985cd12..., gate b01024f3...,
# both rebuilt here with build-wasm.sh to the same hashes and read on testnet as the code entries #26
# uploaded (not uploaded again). Grammar-7 interpreter CDZV4AG4... (69cad1d5...), OZ account 91a2cd56...,
# OZ spending_limit CDH4KOBR... from deployments/oz-policies.json.
# Harness: kept off-repo on the agents' VM (prime-refine/reports/g7-stride-final-evidence/stride-final-probes.ts
# and g2d-probe.ts). Every key is Keypair.random() made in memory for the run; none was written or printed.
#
# Rows: setup and S rows build the accounts; A caps; B rules cited across adapters; C rebind; D grants and
# executor_authorizations; E waits; F cancel; G resubmission; H the Prime binding; I what a null adapter
# holds and custody's gate; J policy-synth's contract-signer refusal and the hazard it guards.
# Error codes: adapter #1 PrimeTarget, #2 AddressNotAllowed, #3 Uncheckable, #5 NotScheduled, #7 NotACanceller,
# #8 NotWhereAgreed, #9 NoGate, #10 NoWait; interpreter #100 deny; OZ account #3002 and #3016 (no rule fits the
# context or its signers), #3221 spending_limit exceeded. In row I2b, #1 is the gate's DestinationNotAllowed.
#
# This is the third run of the harness. Runs 1 and 2 used other fresh instances and are superseded:
# run 1 stopped at G2 with two rows the harness expected wrongly (B5 is refused, where I had expected it to
# run; G2 needed its account funded first); run 2 passed every row but G2d.
# Row G2d below fails on the harness's own criterion: the RPC answers a resent envelope with TRY_AGAIN_LATER,
# and the harness wanted ERROR or DUPLICATE. Nothing moved (the row says so). The second part of this log
# (G2d-0 to G2d-3, another fresh account) sends the same envelope again through the RPC and through Horizon:
# Horizon answers with the original transaction, the balance and the sequence number stay, and the hash
# appears once in the account's history.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- run 3 ---

